WEBVTT

00:00.520 --> 00:03.980
<b>The Sad Dog Warrior I</b>

00:06.360 --> 00:08.700
<i>I am a hunting dog of the demon realm.</i>

00:09.110 --> 00:13.570
<i>As the pet of demon aristocrats, 
I assist with their hunts.</i>

00:32.100 --> 00:34.600
<i>Magical beasts, mythical beasts...</i>

00:34.820 --> 00:37.580
<i>even dragons... I can run them all down.</i>

00:43.990 --> 00:44.990
<i>However...</i>

00:46.780 --> 00:48.620
<i>I've encountered something new.</i>

00:58.340 --> 01:01.480
<i>Someone who'd lost their way 
and wandered here from the human realm...</i>

01:01.480 --> 01:04.360
<i>A beautiful lady wolf.</i>

01:04.960 --> 01:10.080
<i>That world I had always envisioned</i>

01:10.080 --> 01:13.730
<i>Could I have found it?</i>

01:22.600 --> 01:27.220
<i>I lived my days at someone 
else's convenience</i>

01:27.640 --> 01:31.850
<i>Gaining nothing but compromises and regrets</i>

01:31.850 --> 01:33.990
<i>Because I always felt that</i>

01:33.990 --> 01:37.880
<i>Even if it wasn't me standing here</i>

01:37.880 --> 01:41.920
<i>The world would still keep moving forward</i>

01:41.920 --> 01:45.720
<i>Even after I lost it</i>

01:45.720 --> 01:48.000
<i>And its colors faded</i>

01:48.000 --> 01:52.080
<i>The dream from that hazily remembered day</i>

01:52.080 --> 01:54.040
<i>Still remained</i>

01:54.040 --> 01:56.470
<i>The thing that only I can do</i>

01:56.470 --> 01:59.190
<i>And the scenery that I left behind</i>

01:59.190 --> 02:06.710
<i>I was just looking for an answer 
from some other time</i>

02:08.040 --> 02:12.900
<i>Those things that don't change</i>

02:12.900 --> 02:18.480
<i>And those words I protected so carefully</i>

02:18.480 --> 02:23.120
<i>Even if they're all just 
unattractive junk to others</i>

02:23.120 --> 02:31.520
<i>They're all treasures 
that I will never give up</i>

02:39.320 --> 02:41.640
Morlock-san passed away?!

02:42.370 --> 02:43.980
What happened?

02:43.980 --> 02:46.760
That day you went exploring,

02:46.760 --> 02:50.160
when I brought him his meal, 
he wasn't breathing.

02:50.160 --> 02:52.860
What about revival magic? 
Did you take him to a temple?

02:52.860 --> 02:54.020
No.

02:54.020 --> 02:57.440
And the use of a morgue requires 
a large amount of money,

02:57.440 --> 03:00.870
and it isn't really part of our job, so...

03:01.960 --> 03:03.820
Then, where is he now?

03:03.820 --> 03:06.380
I thought that we could keep the body 
from decaying at least,

03:06.380 --> 03:09.340
by keeping it in 
the shade of the shed, but...

03:09.340 --> 03:11.880
A wild dog ate the geezer?

03:11.880 --> 03:13.800
Only a part of him!

03:13.800 --> 03:16.880
But the damage was severe, so...

03:18.700 --> 03:20.520
Is this real?

03:20.520 --> 03:24.870
Revival magic won't succeed 
if the body isn't in good condition.

03:25.350 --> 03:28.020
I've never heard of a case where it worked

03:28.020 --> 03:30.060
after someone had been buried.

03:30.970 --> 03:33.310
I never imagined he'd die from the venom.

03:33.310 --> 03:35.990
Is it because we were late 
in giving him the antidote?

03:35.990 --> 03:39.180
He got better for a little while, 
so I stopped being wary.

03:39.180 --> 03:42.320
And he spread a bunch of honey 
on that bread and ate it, so...

03:42.700 --> 03:46.460
Something this big isn't 
going to fit in my mouth!

03:47.270 --> 03:50.180
He didn't die in our fight 
with that dark spirit.

03:50.180 --> 03:51.840
How could this be his end?

03:55.540 --> 03:56.990
Geezer...

03:57.750 --> 04:01.260
<b>The great mage Morlock</b>

03:57.750 --> 04:01.260
<b>has died</b>

04:01.260 --> 04:04.380
We don't know for sure 
that revival is impossible, right?

04:04.380 --> 04:05.760
Let's dig him up!

04:06.660 --> 04:10.720
Revival magic requires 
a tremendous donation to the church.

04:10.720 --> 04:13.260
And the geezer's stupidly high-level.

04:13.720 --> 04:15.170
It won't be an amount we can pay.

04:15.170 --> 04:16.280
Still!

04:16.280 --> 04:19.980
The more time passes, the more the chances 
of the revival's success drop, right?

04:19.980 --> 04:24.120
We have to dig him up and use Lafa's magic 
to maintain his current condition!

04:24.120 --> 04:25.480
But...

04:27.500 --> 04:29.030
Raelza...

04:29.030 --> 04:34.080
You're always badmouthing him, 
but he's important to you, isn't he?

04:37.960 --> 04:41.960
If there's even the smallest possibility, 
let's do everything we can.

04:42.380 --> 04:44.380
Unlike the world I came from,

04:44.380 --> 04:48.180
in this world, death isn't an absolute ending.

04:50.260 --> 04:53.120
What Saitou is saying is right.

04:53.600 --> 04:55.890
Let's gather the tools we need 
before it gets too late.

04:55.890 --> 04:57.010
Lafa...

04:57.480 --> 05:01.570
I'll go buy what I need 
for the magic from Maevena's shop.

05:01.570 --> 05:05.190
You two go borrow tools 
for digging from the inn.

05:05.190 --> 05:07.080
We'll meet up again before it gets dark!

05:07.080 --> 05:08.220
Will do!

05:10.160 --> 05:14.280
<i>If it had only been the two of us,
we probably would have given up, right?</i>

05:23.210 --> 05:26.680
<b>The Sad Dog Warrior II</b>

05:28.700 --> 05:31.970
<i>On days when there were 
no hunts, I went to her.</i>

05:32.410 --> 05:34.430
<i>We were happy.</i>

05:35.640 --> 05:39.150
<i>That is, until the day my master 
decided upon our next target.</i>

05:39.750 --> 05:41.570
You know...

05:41.570 --> 05:43.440
There's a beautiful wolf...

05:43.440 --> 05:44.950
out there, I hear.

05:44.960 --> 05:46.280
I want it.

05:46.670 --> 05:49.140
I want to stuff and display it.

05:50.610 --> 05:54.750
<i>I made up my mind to help 
her escape to the human realm.</i>

06:03.750 --> 06:07.200
I was told not to damage its pelt.

06:07.200 --> 06:10.220
It's difficult to determine 
the right amount of force, isn't it?

06:11.970 --> 06:15.730
I was told that I can kill this dog.

07:30.020 --> 07:32.340
<i>I wanted to disappear 
and become nothingness.</i>

07:32.940 --> 07:36.800
<i>I was going to try to find a way to die.</i>

07:53.120 --> 07:55.120
It's gotten so late.

07:55.120 --> 07:57.600
Ever since Saitou's Tunnel was discovered,

07:57.600 --> 07:59.480
all the shops are crazy busy.

07:59.480 --> 08:00.140
Huh?

08:02.460 --> 08:04.940
Did they already dig him up?

08:05.840 --> 08:08.420
Where are Raelza and Saitou?

08:13.140 --> 08:15.010
Blast it! That took too long!

08:15.010 --> 08:17.440
Things seemed busy at the inn.

08:18.780 --> 08:20.230
Get down!

08:23.180 --> 08:25.100
Wh-What was that?

08:29.800 --> 08:31.320
A Fiery Heat Blast?

08:31.320 --> 08:32.560
Get behind the rocks!

08:43.160 --> 08:44.300
That's...

08:44.920 --> 08:46.130
an undead?

08:48.080 --> 08:49.550
That robe!

08:49.550 --> 08:51.270
The geezer?

08:56.450 --> 08:57.600
Are you all right?

08:57.600 --> 08:59.230
Why is he attacking us?

08:59.230 --> 09:00.390
I don't know.

09:00.710 --> 09:03.100
His memories were unstable even before this.

09:03.100 --> 09:06.180
It could be that he's lost them completely 
now that he's become an undead.

09:15.020 --> 09:17.440
Blast it. We have no choice but to fight.

09:18.490 --> 09:19.780
Geezer...

09:20.160 --> 09:21.250
I'm sorry!

09:27.390 --> 09:29.290
That wasn't enough to crack it?

09:29.290 --> 09:31.620
Anything other than a magical 
weapon really won't work?

09:31.620 --> 09:32.550
Raelza!

09:32.940 --> 09:33.930
Use this!

09:33.930 --> 09:35.300
Purify your weapon!

09:39.940 --> 09:41.890
The holy water...

09:47.920 --> 09:48.980
This is bad!

09:51.440 --> 09:53.780
Morlock-san, that's Raelza!

10:02.030 --> 10:07.040
That spell came so easily, 
and in the spur of the moment.

10:07.390 --> 10:09.040
That voice...

10:10.580 --> 10:12.880
I'm pretty good.

10:13.850 --> 10:15.220
Geezer!

10:16.140 --> 10:18.670
I'm so glad you're safe!

10:18.670 --> 10:21.760
So this was just a regular undead?

10:22.290 --> 10:25.640
Do you two have a better opinion of me now?

10:25.640 --> 10:29.340
What?!

10:29.700 --> 10:32.360
A-Are you our geezer?

10:32.360 --> 10:33.760
What happened to you?

10:34.350 --> 10:35.640
No idea.

10:35.890 --> 10:40.920
I do remember losing consciousness
 while lying on the bed...

10:43.180 --> 10:45.290
He's turning into Morlock-san!

10:45.600 --> 10:48.440
...but when I woke up...

10:48.440 --> 10:49.410
Huh?

10:49.880 --> 10:51.960
You really are the geezer!

10:51.960 --> 10:53.210
That's so creepy!

10:55.210 --> 10:57.460
A resurrection contract?

10:57.460 --> 10:58.270
That's right.

10:58.270 --> 11:00.690
Even if you die, you'll come back 
to life after a day.

11:00.690 --> 11:02.190
It's high-level magic.

11:02.190 --> 11:04.020
And it's only effective once.

11:04.020 --> 11:07.100
So, Morlock-san had that cast on him?

11:07.100 --> 11:09.390
I don't know. I've forgotten.

11:09.390 --> 11:11.640
Geezer, you really are useless.

11:11.640 --> 11:13.430
Why don't you go catch 
some crayfish or something?

11:14.100 --> 11:16.010
But this is wonderful, isn't it?

11:16.010 --> 11:17.600
He was able to come back to life.

11:17.600 --> 11:21.790
Well, about that. Something's wrong.

11:21.790 --> 11:23.160
Ack! He died!

11:23.160 --> 11:26.660
I haven't died. Probably.

11:27.130 --> 11:28.840
And now he's back again.

11:29.560 --> 11:35.100
I keep coming back, then turning 
into a skeleton over and over again.

11:35.100 --> 11:36.880
That's gross! It's just too creepy!

11:36.880 --> 11:38.310
And...

11:38.310 --> 11:40.880
It's gone. My thingy.

11:41.330 --> 11:42.840
Your thingy?

11:44.200 --> 11:45.680
This!

11:46.100 --> 11:47.030
It's gone!

11:47.030 --> 11:50.390
The dirty old man's dirty old thing is gone!

11:50.390 --> 11:55.640
If I'm like this, I can't play 
with that little succubus anymore!

11:55.640 --> 11:58.160
I mean, the innkeeper did say

11:58.160 --> 12:01.840
that a wild dog had eaten 
a part of his body, but...

12:01.840 --> 12:04.160
Hey, maybe we can think 
about it like this...

12:04.160 --> 12:06.600
The reason his resurrection isn't working...

12:06.600 --> 12:09.160
is because part of his body is missing.

12:09.500 --> 12:12.840
If that's the case, then there's
 nothing we can do.

12:12.840 --> 12:14.920
The dog already ate it.

12:14.920 --> 12:16.750
No!

12:16.750 --> 12:23.410
Not my thingy! It could hold its 
own against Maderaka I's when it was perky!

12:23.740 --> 12:25.680
What? That means...

12:25.680 --> 12:27.270
One maderaka, so that's...

12:27.270 --> 12:30.320
Thirty centimeters? Wow.

12:30.320 --> 12:32.580
Saitou, what's yours like?

12:32.580 --> 12:36.130
Even when it's perky, 
at most it's half a maderaka.

12:37.440 --> 12:39.970
You're pretty small.

12:39.970 --> 12:43.150
Half a maderaka's only 
about this big, you know?

12:43.150 --> 12:45.840
I hate so much about this!

12:45.840 --> 12:48.500
At any rate, what's gone is gone.

12:48.500 --> 12:50.830
You didn't die. Let that be enough.

12:50.830 --> 12:55.590
I don't wanna! Give me my thingy back!

12:55.910 --> 12:58.310
Stop it! I will exorcise you!

12:58.310 --> 13:00.540
Hey! Raelza, help me!

13:00.540 --> 13:02.280
<i>Half a maderaka...</i>

13:02.760 --> 13:05.130
You're thinking of 
something else, aren't you?!

13:05.980 --> 13:07.540
<i>Half a maderaka...</i>

13:07.540 --> 13:09.950
It's great that he came back,

13:09.950 --> 13:12.470
but won't leaving him like this be worrying?

13:12.470 --> 13:14.760
Well, you have a point.

13:14.760 --> 13:18.220
One day, he might stay a skeleton 
and not come back.

13:18.470 --> 13:20.790
I have heard everything!

13:22.160 --> 13:23.190
There he is...

13:23.190 --> 13:25.440
Morlock-san's stalker.

13:25.440 --> 13:27.080
Oh, how tragic!

13:27.080 --> 13:30.450
But now his favorite disciple, 
Gibungle, will lend you his strength.

13:30.840 --> 13:34.450
Do you really know any magic 
that Grandpa doesn't know?

13:34.650 --> 13:37.890
Compared to my master, 
I still have a long ways to go.

13:37.890 --> 13:40.450
However, with this book, perhaps...

13:40.760 --> 13:44.320
Everything about magic is recorded 
within this great encyclopedia of magic...

13:44.320 --> 13:45.970
the Magipedia!

13:46.310 --> 13:47.920
If everything is recorded in there,

13:47.920 --> 13:51.720
then use it when you're looking 
for magic to control time!

13:51.720 --> 13:53.920
According to the Magipedia,

13:53.920 --> 13:57.940
when revival magic fails 
because a part of the body is missing...

13:57.940 --> 14:01.230
then all that needs be done is 
to retrieve the missing part.

14:01.230 --> 14:03.410
But a dog ate it.

14:03.410 --> 14:05.780
Even if the flesh eaten 
has been digested,

14:05.780 --> 14:09.500
it's very likely that the magical energy 
remains within the one who consumed it.

14:10.120 --> 14:13.880
Especially if one possesses power 
at the level of my master.

14:13.880 --> 14:18.000
Which means that if we find the dog 
that ate Grandpa's thingy...

14:18.000 --> 14:20.760
...and successfully 
extract his magical energy,

14:20.760 --> 14:23.540
my master may be able to revive completely.

14:23.540 --> 14:24.360
What?

14:24.360 --> 14:27.000
It's decided, then! Let's find that dog!

14:27.920 --> 14:30.600
I don't know who you are, but let's go!

14:31.230 --> 14:33.140
I'm your apprentice, Gibungle!

14:33.140 --> 14:34.720
Wait!

14:34.720 --> 14:37.570
If it concerns magic, I'm going too!

14:39.190 --> 14:40.830
They left.

14:40.830 --> 14:42.480
We should go too.

14:42.480 --> 14:44.010
Y-Yes...

14:44.010 --> 14:45.810
<i>Half a maderaka...</i>

14:45.810 --> 14:48.630
Oh, he forgot to take his Magipedia.

14:49.780 --> 14:52.690
Who wrote this book?

14:52.690 --> 14:54.780
Some magician from long ago?

14:54.780 --> 14:58.130
By... void rank, first-class Great Mage...

14:58.440 --> 15:00.790
Bergheim Crom?!

15:00.970 --> 15:04.950
The geezer forgot 
that he wrote this himself!

15:05.840 --> 15:09.300
<b>The Sad Dog Warrior III</b>

15:09.310 --> 15:11.460
<i>Half a year after she had died,</i>

15:12.050 --> 15:16.310
<i>my offspring and 
I were living in the human realm.</i>

15:16.930 --> 15:19.260
<i>Here, I am teaching the pup how to hunt...</i>

15:20.020 --> 15:22.720
<i>so that it can live on its own.</i>

15:30.680 --> 15:32.980
<i>I hadn't realized...</i>

15:39.680 --> 15:42.270
<i>that my master had cast
 binding magic upon me.</i>

15:43.020 --> 15:46.710
<i>Those invisible chains 
still had me in their grip.</i>

15:48.400 --> 15:50.850
Can you really find the dog, old man?

15:50.850 --> 15:54.300
Do not underestimate my 
ability with magic detection.

15:54.300 --> 15:57.300
And my name is Gibungle!

15:57.300 --> 16:00.640
My master and I have eaten 
and slept together.

16:00.640 --> 16:03.810
Detecting the scent of his magical 
energy should prove a simple feat.

16:04.260 --> 16:07.320
Can you please stop saying things 
that could be misunderstood?

16:07.320 --> 16:10.770
Well, I know Grandpa really well. too!

16:10.770 --> 16:12.030
What did you say?!

16:12.030 --> 16:13.120
No, you!

16:13.120 --> 16:15.880
I'm hoping to find it quickly.

16:15.880 --> 16:20.700
I can't detect my own magical energy, you know.

16:20.700 --> 16:22.850
Leave it to me!

16:22.850 --> 16:24.950
I will begin my magic detection immediately!

16:24.950 --> 16:26.480
No fair starting ahead of me!

16:26.480 --> 16:27.300
I'll do it too!

16:42.680 --> 16:46.440
Grandpa, your magic 
is so strong, I can't detect it.

16:46.440 --> 16:49.420
Even weakened, it's still this strong.

16:49.420 --> 16:52.940
I never imagined that he himself 
would become an obstacle in this.

16:54.580 --> 16:56.200
Hey, Gramps!

16:56.200 --> 16:57.520
It's been a while!

16:57.520 --> 16:59.660
I haven't seen you 
in the great labyrinth lately.

16:59.660 --> 17:01.120
Oh, it's my dear elf!

17:02.890 --> 17:04.430
Ninia, exorcise it!

17:04.430 --> 17:06.500
Undead, perish now!

17:06.500 --> 17:09.410
No, don't!

17:12.250 --> 17:14.920
A dog ate the corpse?

17:14.920 --> 17:18.160
If we can't use magic detection, 
I don't know what we'll do.

17:18.160 --> 17:20.930
Maybe we'll leave Grandpa 
with Raelza and Saitou.

17:21.280 --> 17:22.910
I wonder if they're still at the inn.

17:22.910 --> 17:24.930
Those two are right over there.

17:25.640 --> 17:27.680
Stop flirting with each other!

17:29.640 --> 17:30.520
A poster?

17:30.790 --> 17:31.740
Yes.

17:31.740 --> 17:36.110
The innkeeper said it had a distinctive 
cross-shaped scar on its forehead.

17:36.110 --> 17:38.210
Huh? Saitou, did you draw this?

17:38.210 --> 17:40.280
It's really good.

17:40.280 --> 17:44.590
In my last world, I took on jobs
looking for cats and dogs, too.

17:44.590 --> 17:48.270
I can't use magic, 
so this is about all I can do.

17:48.880 --> 17:50.800
Saitou...

17:50.800 --> 17:54.090
Give me one. I'll help put them up.

17:55.470 --> 17:57.310
This one is poorly drawn.

17:57.310 --> 17:59.170
No artistic sense at all.

17:59.170 --> 18:01.090
Well, excuse me!

18:01.090 --> 18:02.910
This dog...

18:03.350 --> 18:04.710
You recognize it?

18:05.110 --> 18:08.100
I haven't seen it myself, but...

18:08.100 --> 18:12.110
<b>Requesting destruction
 of undead</b>

18:08.100 --> 18:12.110
<b>Please find the
sword I dropped in
 the great labyrinth</b>

18:08.330 --> 18:12.110
You know how there are work 
requests posted on the tavern wall?

18:12.110 --> 18:13.400
Among them was one that said,

18:13.400 --> 18:17.160
"A huge dog with a cross-shaped scar 
on its head is attacking people."

18:17.160 --> 18:19.190
"Requesting its elimination."

18:19.190 --> 18:21.610
It was on the outskirts 
of the town to the west.

18:21.610 --> 18:22.930
Let's go right now!

18:22.930 --> 18:25.360
That's close to where 
Morlock-san was buried!

18:25.360 --> 18:27.450
You're not taking the job?

18:27.450 --> 18:29.760
The pay is low.

18:29.760 --> 18:31.830
And undead show up in that area, too.

18:31.830 --> 18:33.120
It's not worth it.

18:33.120 --> 18:34.480
I see.

18:34.880 --> 18:38.250
In that case, Master, 
let's head there immediately!

18:38.250 --> 18:43.640
Ninia, once I'm back to normal,
will you come and play with me?

18:43.640 --> 18:44.640
I will not.

18:47.310 --> 18:49.140
Let's head out right now.

18:49.440 --> 18:52.900
<b>The Sad Dog Warrior IV</b>

18:53.160 --> 18:56.430
<i>Day by day, my body grew weaker.</i>

19:09.800 --> 19:11.930
<i>I didn't want to die.</i>

19:13.860 --> 19:18.350
<i>Until the pup could survive 
on its own, I couldn't die.</i>

19:31.490 --> 19:34.360
<i>I sensed incredibly powerful magical energy.</i>

19:34.690 --> 19:38.360
<i>I wanted to live! No matter what it took...</i>

19:52.920 --> 19:54.710
<i>Something's wrong!</i>

19:59.310 --> 20:03.370
<i>All that magical energy 
is rampaging inside me!</i>

20:04.530 --> 20:05.900
<i>I...</i>

20:06.830 --> 20:08.610
<i>I am...</i>

20:10.480 --> 20:12.170
A wild dog?

20:24.040 --> 20:28.410
<i>I am a hunting dog of the demon realm!</i>

20:41.480 --> 20:45.680
The dog that ate part of my 
master's body is in this vicinity.

20:45.680 --> 20:47.100
A dog, huh?

20:47.100 --> 20:48.720
Feeling a little hesitant?

20:48.720 --> 20:50.670
I know you love dogs, Raelza.

20:50.670 --> 20:53.150
It isn't certain that we'll have to kill it.

20:53.150 --> 20:58.940
Someone of my master's caliber may have 
a method to retrieve just his magical energy.

20:58.940 --> 21:00.630
And... where is my master?

21:00.630 --> 21:02.330
Saitou is gone too!

21:03.190 --> 21:05.790
Morlock-san, are you all right?

21:05.790 --> 21:08.650
I'll be all right once I rest a little.

21:08.650 --> 21:10.640
The others walk so fast, don't they?

21:10.640 --> 21:13.740
Well, this is a perfect opportunity.

21:15.170 --> 21:16.590
Say, Saitou...

21:16.590 --> 21:21.120
What do you think of Raelza?

21:21.120 --> 21:23.760
What? Why are you asking this now?

21:23.760 --> 21:27.620
Raelza is, of course, 
a dependable party member.

21:27.620 --> 21:30.340
Not like that.

21:30.340 --> 21:33.690
What do you think of her as a regular girl?

21:33.690 --> 21:34.900
What?

21:37.460 --> 21:41.050
When I first met Raelza...

21:41.520 --> 21:45.270
She was about ten years old.

21:48.190 --> 21:51.580
Before she was old enough to remember him,

21:51.580 --> 21:55.530
her father died while killing a wolf.

21:56.340 --> 21:58.480
And the mother who was all she had left

21:58.480 --> 22:00.900
went out into the mountains 
in the winter

22:00.900 --> 22:02.980
looking for food and never returned.

22:04.000 --> 22:08.360
She may have fought 
the wolf's mate and died.

22:08.360 --> 22:10.600
That's what Raelza said.

22:11.830 --> 22:15.540
As Raelza waited for her mother, 
who would never come home,

22:15.540 --> 22:17.790
she lived strong-willed and undaunted.

22:19.280 --> 22:21.120
And then...

22:21.970 --> 22:26.530
She met a wolf pup 
that was just skin and bones.

22:33.080 --> 22:37.720
She said that she felt they 
were alike somehow.

22:38.750 --> 22:44.290
And she told me that they 
lived together for many years.

22:45.680 --> 22:49.160
But I met her after all of that.

22:50.000 --> 22:54.510
After we met, she came to live 
with me as an adventurer.

22:54.960 --> 22:57.380
She's family to me.

22:57.650 --> 22:59.520
Like a daughter.

23:02.270 --> 23:04.150
The truth is...

23:04.150 --> 23:05.780
Since a while ago,

23:05.780 --> 23:11.440
I've felt my body's 
regeneration growing weaker.

23:12.820 --> 23:14.660
Morlock-san!

23:15.280 --> 23:19.580
Since the worst may very 
well happen, I want to say this.

23:20.800 --> 23:23.920
If you're all right with it...

23:23.920 --> 23:28.990
would you be so good 
as to take my daughter, Raelza?
